From e658e419e87404942177830126773e6d5ae56bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(standings): configurable team/speaker precedence (Stage
 3, C1)

- New TeamMetricId / SpeakerMetricId types and TournamentPreferences fields:
  teamStandingsPrecedence, teamStandingsExtra, speakerStandingsPrecedence,
  speakerStandingsExtra, speakerTrim.
- src/lib/standings/metrics.ts: pure metric functions for all 14 team metrics
  (wins, points, speaks_sum/avg/ind_avg/stddev, margin_sum/avg,
  draw_strength_wins/speaks, firsts/seconds/thirds, pullups) and 7 speaker
  metrics (speaks_sum/avg/stddev/trimmed_mean, speeches_count, reply_sum/avg).
- src/lib/standings/precedence.ts: resolves the configured chain (falling back
  to the exact legacy default per format), a generic compareByPrecedence /
  assignSharedRanks pair usable for both teams and speakers.
- calculator.ts rewritten to accumulate the richer per-round data (opponent
  ids for draw strength, pulled-up flag, individual scores) and rank off the
  resolved precedence, while keeping every existing field/shape so
  calculateBreaks and generatePowerPairedDraw (which just consume its output)
  inherit the configured precedence automatically.
- Config page: ordered add/remove/reorder editor for team + speaker
  precedence, checkbox editor for 'extra' (shown, not ranked) metrics, and a
  speaker-trim input.
- DebateTeamSlot.pulledUp and TeamStandingRow.roundResults[].opponentTeamIds
  added for other stages to populate (C2 draw generator, C6 elimination).
- Tests: new precedence.test.ts (12 cases: default-reproduces-legacy for both
  formats, custom precedence reorders results, draw strength, pullups,
  speaker trim, tie-sharing). All 47 pre-existing tests still pass unchanged.
